# Optional defaults for the Connect dialogs. Copy to .env, which Git ignores and packaging excludes.
# Settings you save in the app take precedence over these values.
# IDs are not secrets. Never put access tokens or Entra client secrets here.
# A2A and REST: your public-client app registration.
WORKIQ_TENANT_ID=
WORKIQ_CLIENT_ID=
# Remote MCP: leave empty to use Microsoft's published MCP client.
WORKIQ_MCP_TENANT_ID=
WORKIQ_MCP_CLIENT_ID=
# Harness model for the MCP tab: an Azure OpenAI or Foundry resource or project URL, or any OpenAI-compatible base URL.
# It signs in with Microsoft Entra ID (DefaultAzureCredential) on Azure endpoints, or with WORKIQ_LLM_API_KEY below.
WORKIQ_LLM_ENDPOINT=
# The model name; on Azure, the deployment name.
WORKIQ_LLM_DEPLOYMENT=
# responses (the default; streams reasoning summaries) or chat (Chat Completions, which most providers offer).
WORKIQ_LLM_API=
# Optional: low, medium or high to show reasoning summaries. Empty uses the model default.
WORKIQ_LLM_REASONING=
# Optional: the API key for WORKIQ_LLM_ENDPOINT, needed for endpoints outside Azure. When set, the model starts with
# API-key authentication. The app sends it only to that endpoint's host, holds it in memory and never writes it to
# its settings file. It is a secret, so keep .env private.
WORKIQ_LLM_API_KEY=
